    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\nI implemented the daily-registration limit rule following the repository's existing conventions:\n\n- **`OwnerRepository.countByRegistrationDate(LocalDate)`** \u2014 new count method (Spring Data JPA derives it automatically; explicitly implemented in the JPA and JDBC impls to match `countByCity`).\n- **`ClinicService`/`ClinicServiceImpl.countOwnersByRegistrationDate(...)`** \u2014 a thin read-only facade method mirroring `countOwnersByCity`.\n- **`DailyRegistrationLimiter`** \u2014 a new single-responsibility `@Component` (modeled on `CityCapacityChecker`) that reports whether the server's current date has already reached `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100` registered owners, using the injected `Clock` so it agrees with `RegistrationDateDefaulter`.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 checks the limiter alongside the other create guards and returns `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` when the day is at capacity, before the owner is saved (so it doesn't count itself).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100, expect the 101st rejected with 429) passes, and no existing tests broke.",
